# API_HOST is a single staging DNS name set in deploy/.env. A hostname site
# address enables Caddy's automatic certificate issuance and renewal.
#
# [Q11] WEB_HOST (optional, deploy/.env) is the website's DNS name, and it
# shares this site on purpose. Caddy substitutes {$NAME} before it parses, and
# an unset or empty WEB_HOST expands to nothing: here that leaves API_HOST as
# the only address. A separate `{$WEB_HOST} { ... }` block would lose its only
# address instead, be read as a misplaced global-options block, and fail the
# WHOLE file, the API site included. Requests are split on the API host, which
# is always set; every other host on this site is the website, and with
# WEB_HOST unset there is no other host. The website sends its own security
# headers (apps/web/next.config.ts); none are added or overridden here.
#
# [STORE-1] API_ALIAS_HOST (optional, deploy/.env) is a SECOND DNS name for the
# same API. The store build of the app is fixed to the production API name; until
# a production stack exists, that name points at this stack. It gets its own
# certificate like any site address, and it MUST be in the @api matcher: any
# host missing from the matcher is served the website. Unset or empty, it
# expands to nothing and this file is exactly what it was without it.
#
# [Item 8] WEB_ALIAS_HOSTS (optional, deploy/.env) is a space-separated list of
# extra DNS names for the WEBSITE — the public swiftgy.com and www.swiftgy.com
# while no production stack exists. Each gets its own certificate and, being
# absent from the @api matcher, reaches the website. www is redirected to the
# apex by the website itself (apps/web/next.config.ts), which keeps the app-link
# files on www unredirected; no redirect belongs here. Unset or empty, it
# expands to nothing and this file is exactly what it was without it.
{$API_HOST} {$API_ALIAS_HOST} {$WEB_HOST} {$WEB_ALIAS_HOSTS} {
    encode zstd gzip
    @api host {$API_HOST} {$API_ALIAS_HOST}
    handle @api {
        @metrics path /metrics
        respond @metrics 403
        reverse_proxy api:3000
    }
    handle {
        reverse_proxy web:3000
    }
}
